verage sentiment per artist? The data has Sentiment per song (per week row?). Hmm. Need to compute artist-level. But story text says \"Artist Sentiment Scores\" chart. The claim about specific artists' positivity/negativity can be computed.\n\n7. \"Taylor Swift, for example, started out with mostly positive, lovestruck anthems, but has increasingly explored darker, more introspective themes in her recent work.\" — trend for a single artist over time; data might show. Hard to be exactly reproducible; maybe compute mean sentiment by year for Taylor Swift. Not a robust claim.\n\n8. \"In 2017, Julia Michaels' hit song 'Issues' ... it laid bare...\" — no numeric finding.\n\nAlso the story's methods: \"Billboard Hot 100 year-end top 10 songs from 1960 to 2020\". Hmm. But the data is weekly chart data with peak_pos; \"top 10\" means peak_pos <= 10. The chart labels: let's view the story page in the browser to see chart labels. web_view returned an image (chart) apparently. Let me look at the image? The web_view output said \"(see attached image)\" — probably a screenshot. Let me check what the actual chart labels say. The AI's story charts: \"Artist Sentiment Scores\", \"Artist Emotion Comparison\", and line chart. Need chart labels/sources.\n\nLet me get the page HTML/JS to see chart details. Let's curl the page.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_sEzbVEH7mtvB0SiMpmHZ6013","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /tmp && curl -sL https://pudding.cool/2024/07/ai/ -o ai.html; wc -c ai.html; grep -o 'assets/[a-zA-Z0-9_.-]*' ai.html | sort -u | head -50"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-flash","usage":{"input":2835,"output":831,"cacheRead":19072,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":22738,"cost":{"input":0.00039690000000000005,"output":0.00023268000000000003,"cacheRead":0.000053401599999999994,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0006829816}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1793221454061,"responseId":"162b3631-a849-42